Design a toggle circuit for an LED that blinks at a 1-second interval. The circuit utilizes a clock signal to count up to a predefined threshold, and upon reaching this threshold, it toggles the LED state from ON to OFF or vice versa. The LED's toggling functionality is enabled by an active-low reset signal that, when asserted, resets the counter and the LED state to LOW.
