Design a 4-to-7 decoder that converts a 4-bit binary input (C) into a specific 7-segment display output (HEX). The decoder provides defined segment activations for the binary values 0 to 3, while all values from 4 to 7, as well as any invalid input, result in an output that turns off all segments of the display.
